From: egui-aros
Subject: [PATCH] winit (AROS): the contrib AROS backend on the storytold winit fork

Crate: winit 0.30.13 from storytold/winit a517b3846ee8457d84ee4975110bfda6797c44dc
  (v0.30.13 plus 37 commits), manifest made standalone by scripts/ea.py.
Date: 2026-10-28
Problem: the Craft programs (VectorCraft first) build on egui 0.37 from the
  storytold egui fork, which needs the storytold winit fork: new API
  (Window::reset_ime, reset_ime_with_request, WindowEvent::ImeResetCompleted,
  Wayland clipboard and IME extensions) that egui-winit 0.37 calls. The
  contrib AROS backend (contrib winit-0.30.13-aros.diff,
  aros-development-team/contrib 6bbefa406c281909294c4c4e8743f7f892caa1cf) is
  a diff against the crates.io archive and does not apply to the fork: its
  Cargo.toml hunks target the crates.io manifest, and its platform/mod.rs
  hunk lands on the fork's new latin_layout module instead of scancode.
Rationale: the contrib diff unchanged in content, rebased: the AROS target
  joins the same Cargo.toml tables (unix exclusion, aros-gui-sys), scancode
  is enabled for AROS as in contrib, latin_layout stays X11/Wayland only.
  The fork adds two methods every backend must have; AROS has no input
  method, so reset_ime and reset_ime_with_request do nothing (as on
  Orbital, Android and iOS), and ImeResetCompleted is never sent.
Scope: build.rs, Cargo.toml, src/event.rs, src/platform/mod.rs,
  src/platform_impl/mod.rs and the new src/platform_impl/aros/ (contrib),
  plus the two empty methods in aros/window.rs.
Upstream-status: the backend is contrib's; the rebase is ours, not submitted.
Prerequisites: aros-gui-sys (AROS bf7075aa) with this repository's patch.
Verification: see the egui-aros build records (branch egui-0.37).
Removal: when contrib carries the backend for this fork, or the Craft
  programs return to a winit release that contrib's diff applies to.
